OL,3,ARayner criticises visa rule proposals
OL,4,Aahead of Labour conference
OL,5,
OL,6,FHousing Secretary Angela Rayner has
OL,7,Fsaid she is concerned about Labour's
OL,8,Fproposals to change visa rules, which
OL,9,Fwould make it harder for foreign
OL,10,Fworkers to secure permanent residency
OL,11,Fin the UK.
OL,13,FIn an interview with the Times ahead of
OL,14,FLabour's annual conference, Rayner
OL,15,Fquestioned Home Secretary Shabana
OL,16,FMahmood's plans, saying they are unfair
OL,17,Fbecause they "change the goalposts".
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1790421955
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ARayner criticises visa rule proposals
OL,4,Aahead of Labour conference
OL,5,
OL,6,FUnder the proposals, most migrants
OL,7,Fwould have to wait 10 years to qualify
OL,8,Ffor residency - instead of the current
OL,9,Ffive - while foreign workers on health
OL,10,Fand social care visas would face a
OL,11,F15-year wait.
OL,13,FMahmood said the government would make
OL,14,Fa decision on the immigration overhaul
OL,15,Fby the end of the year.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/39
